<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Config:etc/system_file.xsd">
    <system>
        <section id="mage_obsidian_frontend">
            <!--
                Same `seo` group MageObsidian_ModernFrontend declares (groups merge
                by id), so head metadata sits next to the JSON-LD switch instead of
                in a tree of its own. Every field is a toggle on purpose: a store
                that already runs an SEO extension turns off the half it duplicates.
            -->
            <group id="seo" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="30"
                   showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>SEO</label>
                <field id="canonical_enabled" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="20"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Emit a Canonical URL</label>
                    <comment>Adds a rel=canonical to every page that does not already have one. Magento only emits it for catalog pages, and only with the catalog SEO flags on; CMS pages, the home page and search results never get one. A canonical set by the core or another extension is never overwritten.</comment>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <config_path>mage_obsidian/seo/canonical_enabled</config_path>
                </field>
                <field id="canonical_query_params" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="30"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Query Parameters Kept in the Canonical</label>
                    <comment>Comma-separated. Every other parameter is dropped, tracking ones included. Leave `p` and `q` in unless pagination and search results should collapse onto a single URL.</comment>
                    <config_path>mage_obsidian/seo/canonical_query_params</config_path>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="canonical_enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="social_meta_enabled" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="40"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Emit Open Graph and Twitter Card Metadata</label>
                    <comment>Adds og:* and twitter:* derived from the page's own title, description and imagery. Properties another block already writes are complemented, not duplicated.</comment>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <config_path>mage_obsidian/seo/social_meta_enabled</config_path>
                </field>
                <field id="social_image" translate="label comment" type="image" sortOrder="50"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Fallback Share Image</label>
                    <comment>Used where the page has no imagery of its own. Falls back to the store logo when empty. 1200x630 or larger.</comment>
                    <backend_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Backend\Image</backend_model>
                    <base_url type="media" scope_info="1">mage_obsidian/seo</base_url>
                    <upload_dir config="system/filesystem/media" scope_info="1">mage_obsidian/seo</upload_dir>
                    <config_path>mage_obsidian/seo/social_image</config_path>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="social_meta_enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="twitter_site" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="60"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Twitter Account</label>
                    <comment>The @handle credited on the card. Left empty, twitter:site is not emitted.</comment>
                    <config_path>mage_obsidian/seo/twitter_site</config_path>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="social_meta_enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="meta_description_fallback" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="70"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Derive the Meta Description from the Page</label>
                    <comment>When a product or category has no meta description of its own, one is summarised from its content instead of repeating the store default on every page.</comment>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <config_path>mage_obsidian/seo/meta_description_fallback</config_path>
                </field>
                <field id="robots_directives" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="80"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Extra Robots Directives</label>
                    <comment>Comma-separated, appended to the store's robots value. Skipped entirely on pages that are NOINDEX. Clear the field to leave the meta robots exactly as Magento wrote it.</comment>
                    <config_path>mage_obsidian/seo/robots_directives</config_path>
                </field>
                <field id="manifest_enabled" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="90"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Serve a Web App Manifest</label>
                    <comment>Publishes a manifest built from the store name, base URL, logo and favicon, and links it from the head.</comment>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <config_path>mage_obsidian/seo/manifest_enabled</config_path>
                </field>
                <field id="manifest_display" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="100"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Manifest Display Mode</label>
                    <source_model>MageObsidian\Storefront\Model\Seo\Source\ManifestDisplayOptions</source_model>
                    <config_path>mage_obsidian/seo/manifest_display</config_path>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="manifest_enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="manifest_theme_color" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="110"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Manifest Theme Colour</label>
                    <comment>CSS colour the browser paints its own chrome with.</comment>
                    <config_path>mage_obsidian/seo/manifest_theme_color</config_path>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="manifest_enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="manifest_background_color" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="120"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Manifest Background Colour</label>
                    <comment>CSS colour shown while the installed app starts.</comment>
                    <config_path>mage_obsidian/seo/manifest_background_color</config_path>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="manifest_enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="appearance" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="30"
                   showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Appearance</label>
                <comment>Lets the shopper pick a light or dark storefront, or follow their system. Off by default: a storefront only gets a dark appearance once its own catalogue imagery and brand have been checked against one.</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Enable the Appearance Selector</label>
                    <comment>Turned off, the control is not rendered and the storefront always uses the
                        light appearance, whatever the shopper's system prefers.</comment>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <config_path>mage_obsidian/appearance/enabled</config_path>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="speculation" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="40"
                   showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Speculative Loading</label>
                <comment>Lets the browser start loading an internal link before it is clicked.</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Enable Speculative Loading</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <config_path>mage_obsidian/speculation/enabled</config_path>
                </field>
                <field id="mode" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="20"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Mode</label>
                    <comment>Prefetch downloads the document. Prerender also runs it — faster, but it
                        spends a full page render on a destination the visitor may never open, and it
                        executes analytics early unless they handle prerendering.</comment>
                    <source_model>MageObsidian\Storefront\Model\Speculation\Source\ModeOptions</source_model>
                    <config_path>mage_obsidian/speculation/mode</config_path>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="eagerness" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="30"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Eagerness</label>
                    <comment>How early the browser acts on the hint. Higher levels preload sooner and
                        load more pages nobody visits.</comment>
                    <source_model>MageObsidian\Storefront\Model\Speculation\Source\EagernessOptions</source_model>
                    <config_path>mage_obsidian/speculation/eagerness</config_path>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="exclude_paths" translate="label comment" type="textarea" sortOrder="40"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Exclude URL Patterns</label>
                    <comment>One per line. Each token must stay within a single path segment —
                        anything containing a slash is dropped, because a URL pattern group cannot
                        span one.</comment>
                    <config_path>mage_obsidian/speculation/exclude_paths</config_path>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="exclude_extensions" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="50"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Exclude File Extensions</label>
                    <comment>Comma-separated.</comment>
                    <config_path>mage_obsidian/speculation/exclude_extensions</config_path>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="exclude_selectors" translate="label comment" type="textarea" sortOrder="60"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1" canRestore="1">
                    <label>Exclude Selectors</label>
                    <comment>One CSS selector per line. Links matching them are never preloaded.</comment>
                    <config_path>mage_obsidian/speculation/exclude_selectors</config_path>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
            </group>
        </section>
    </system>
</config>
